.TH MALFERMA-LIBRO 1 "2026-10-18" "Malferma Libro 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
malferma-libro \- GTK ebook reader with OPDS catalogs and offline narration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B malferma-libro
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RB [ \-\- ]
.RI [ FILE ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Malferma Libro is a GTK 4 and libadwaita reader for Debian 13.
It imports EPUB, FB2, FB2.ZIP, TXT, HTML/XHTML, Markdown, PDF, DjVu and CBZ
into a local library.
Reading positions, bookmarks and settings are stored locally.
PDF and DjVu retain their page layout; CBZ uses image pages.
EPUB, FB2, TXT, HTML/XHTML and Markdown are presented as text.
Public OPDS 1.x catalogs can be browsed to download books.
.PP
The first group in the main menu opens My books, Reading and Online libraries;
the default shortcuts are Ctrl+1, Ctrl+2 and Ctrl+3.
The table of contents preserves
chapter and subsection hierarchy and groups notes separately. EPUB entries
with fragment targets navigate to the corresponding position within a chapter.
FB2 notes remain available through the table of contents.
.PP
The header groups opening and navigation, book tools, day/night and fullscreen,
and accessibility and menu controls. Text-size controls are available in
Accessibility. One pair of previous/next controls remains in the header;
the table of contents selects chapters. Page tools appear only for PDF,
DjVu and CBZ. Keyboard shortcuts and mouse gestures remain available.
.PP
The window uses a thin border and a light shadow. Maximized and fullscreen
windows hide the outer border. Edge resizing remains available; high-contrast
mode keeps the outline visible.
.SH BOOK COVERS
Covers are selected automatically from embedded EPUB/FB2 images, the first
valid image among at most the first 32 CBZ page candidates, or image URLs
provided by an OPDS catalog. Thumbnails are prepared in the background and
saved in the local covers/ cache. Library rows and the continue-reading card
show them; catalog images are requested only for visible rows.
Missing, invalid or unreachable covers use a standard book-icon placeholder
without preventing reading. Failed remote requests are remembered for the
session; restarting and opening the catalog permits another attempt.
.PP
Embedded and OPDS covers accept PNG and JPEG up to 4 MiB, with each dimension at most
4096 pixels and at most 4 MiPixels in total. No ISBN- or title-based requests
to external cover-search services are made. Vector application artwork
requires the Debian librsvg2-common loader package.
CBZ source-page limits are separate; its cover is scaled to at most 1024
pixels on the longest edge and saved as PNG.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print concise help and exit without loading GTK.
Russian, German or Ukrainian help is used for the corresponding locales;
all other locales use English.
.TP
.BR \-\-manual [=LANG]
Print the complete bundled user guide and exit without loading GTK.
The guide is available in Russian, English, German and Ukrainian.
Without an explicit language, the locale environment selects Russian,
German or Ukrainian when appropriate, with English as the fallback.
Use
.BR \-\-manual=ru ,
.BR \-\-manual=en ,
.BR \-\-manual=de
or
.B \-\-manual=uk
to select a language explicitly. No browser or network connection is used.
.PP
In the graphical guide, the language selector defaults to automatic selection,
which follows interface-language changes immediately and uses English for
other interface languages. Any of the four guide languages can also be selected.
.TP
.B \-\-license
Print the full bundled GNU GPL version 3 text and exit without loading GTK.
The code and logo/icon artwork are licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later;
bundled fonts retain their own licenses.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the application name and version without loading GTK.
.TP
.B \-\-
End option processing. All following arguments are filenames, including names
beginning with a hyphen or matching an informational option.
.PP
Only one informational mode may be selected per invocation.
Informational modes do not open books. Unknown options are rejected.
.SH LIBRARY AND CONTINUING
The Continue Reading card returns to the last successfully opened book and
its saved position. Importing a file alone does not replace that book.
Reopening it automatically at startup is an optional preference, disabled
by default. An explicit file-open request takes precedence.
.PP
The library header has status filters and sorting by recent opening, author,
or title. The per-book menu can set Not started, Reading or Finished.
Opening a book marked Not started marks it Reading; reaching the end does not mark it
Finished automatically. Saved progress and the explicit status are separate.
.SH PAGE NUMBERS
A compact counter at the bottom of the reading area shows pages for the
whole book and updates during scrolling and navigation. If visible text
spans several reference pages, it shows a range, such as Pages 12–13 of 640.
EPUB, FB2, TXT, HTML/XHTML and Markdown use continuous reference pages of
1800 Unicode characters, including spaces and line breaks. Chapters are
counted consecutively, without empty pages or padding at chapter boundaries.
Font, line spacing and window size do not change page numbers or the total
page count. These numbers do not refer to a particular printed edition.
PDF and DjVu retain their original document pages; CBZ uses images in
reading order. Zoom and scrolling within an image do not change its number.
.SH WHOLE-BOOK SEARCH
Search checks every chapter, or lazily extracts PDF/DjVu page text without
rasterizing the book. Results contain chapter/page names and excerpts.
Typing does not change the reading position. Select a result, press Enter
for the next match, or Shift+Enter for the previous match.
The return button restores the position where searching began in that book.
.PP
At most 200 results are displayed. A truncation notice asks for a more specific
query when additional matches exist. Case-insensitive matching preserves
original Unicode selection offsets, including casefold expansions.
Image-only pages cannot be searched; OCR is not provided.
CBZ has no text layer, text search or narration.
.SH BOOKMARKS AND NOTES
Bookmarks show a chapter title or a one-based PDF/DjVu page number and excerpt.
For a fixed-layout page the excerpt uses selected text, or the start of the
text layer; the saved position is the image viewport, not a text offset.
Notes can be added or edited from each bookmark row, up to 2000 characters.
An empty note removes its text. Editing cannot target a different book or
a bookmark that has been removed.
CBZ bookmarks save the page and image scroll position with a page-number label.
.SH BACKGROUND ACTIONS
The header's operation list shows available progress and cancellation controls
for imports, opening, search, rendering and network actions.
Cancellation is cooperative: an already blocked network request or external
decoder need not stop instantly. Already committed imports and other saved
changes remain. Errors offer Retry where supported; a missing file can offer
a new file-selection action.
.SH KEYBOARD
The bindings below are defaults. The main menu's Keyboard shortcuts reference
shows the active profile. Normal GTK commands such as Escape are independent
of the profile.
These shortcuts apply to the main window. Reading actions, including adding
a bookmark and stopping narration, require the active reader section and an
open book. Text inputs and dialogs retain their normal GTK keyboard behavior.
.TP
.B Ctrl+O / Ctrl+F / Ctrl+comma
Open books / search the current section / open preferences.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+A
Open the Accessibility menu, including when the header is hidden in fullscreen.
Ctrl+Shift+Ф also works with the Russian keyboard layout.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+D
Switch both the application and book page between day and night appearance.
Ctrl+Shift+В also works with the Russian keyboard layout.
.TP
.B Ctrl+1 / Ctrl+2 / Ctrl+3
Show the library / reader / OPDS catalogs.
.TP
.B Ctrl+B
Add a bookmark at the current reading position.
.TP
.B Ctrl+minus / Ctrl+plus / Ctrl+0
Decrease / increase / reset text size or PDF/DjVu/CBZ zoom.
.TP
.B Alt+Left / Alt+Right
Previous / next chapter or document page.
.TP
.B F9 / F11
Toggle the table of contents / fullscreen mode.
.TP
.B F10
Reveal a hidden header and move keyboard focus to its controls.
.TP
.B Escape
Close a popup, cancel an active mouse gesture, or leave fullscreen.
.TP
.B Space / Ctrl+Shift+S
Play or pause narration when focus is in the reading area / stop narration.
Space does not replace normal input or focused-button behavior.
.TP
.B F1 / Ctrl+question-mark
Open the offline manual / keyboard shortcut reference.
The latter is usually Ctrl+Shift+slash.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Close the main window.
.PP
Opening a book focuses the reading area for immediate keyboard scrolling.
Click the text or page image to return after using other controls. Toolbar
buttons, the table of contents, search field, document text layer, other
inputs and open menus or dialogs retain their normal key behavior.
.TP
.B Up / Down
Scroll a small distance up / down without changing chapters.
.TP
.B Left / Right
Previous / next page. In text books, scroll by 90% of the viewport height
with a 10% overlap; at an already reached boundary, open the bottom of the
previous chapter or the top of the next one. In PDF, DjVu and CBZ, open the
adjacent document page at its top, even when zoomed and scrolled.
Directions stay the same in LTR and RTL books: Left goes back, Right forward.
Page numbers remain continuous across the whole book.
.TP
.B Page Up / Page Down
Scroll by 90% of the viewport height. At an already reached boundary, open
the bottom of the previous chapter or page, or the top of the next one.
Navigation stops at the book's ends.
.TP
.B Home / End
Go to the beginning / end of the current chapter or document page.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Home / Ctrl+End
Go to the beginning / end of the whole book. A custom binding for the same
combination takes precedence.
.PP
Tab, Shift+Tab, text selection and copying retain normal GTK behavior.
Shift variants of navigation keys retain text selection. Numeric-keypad
navigation works with Num Lock off; with Num Lock on, digits remain digits.
Reading navigation is also listed in the shortcut reference; a Ctrl combination
replaced by a custom binding is not listed as a scrolling command.
.SH SHORTCUT PREFERENCES
Open Settings, then Keyboard shortcuts. Mode selects Default or Custom;
Custom inherits every default binding that has not been changed.
Use Change shortcut beside an action and press the new key combination.
Disable removes the action's binding; Default restores its original keys.
These changes are staged until Save applies and persists them immediately.
Cancel or Escape discards the edit.
.PP
A replacement removes the action's old default aliases, including Russian
layout aliases. Conflicting bindings are rejected, including Latin/Cyrillic
aliases on the same physical key. Escape, Tab, normal Ctrl+C/V/X/A/Z/Y editing,
ordinary typing and unmodified navigation keys are reserved.
Use Ctrl, Alt or a function key; Super combinations are unsupported.
Unmodified Space is allowed only for narration with focus in the reading area.
.PP
Changing Mode takes effect immediately. Returning to Default retains the
saved Custom profile. Reset all shortcuts immediately clears custom bindings
and selects Default without changing other preferences.
.SH DAY AND NIGHT
The top-bar day/night button or default Ctrl+Shift+D switches the window
and book page together between light and dark appearance. The choice is saved;
reading position is retained and paused narration does not resume by itself.
The original appearance of PDF/DjVu/CBZ image pages remains unchanged.
System appearance and sepia remain available in the full preferences.
.SH MOUSE GESTURES
Hold the right mouse button in the reading area and drag left for the next
chapter or page, or right for the previous one. Navigation occurs on release.
Short, vertical and diagonal movements do not turn a page.
Gestures can be disabled in accessibility preferences.
.SH FULLSCREEN HEADER
During fullscreen reading the header can hide after about two seconds of
inactivity. Move the pointer into the top 24 logical pixels, use F10, or use
Tab to reveal it. Toolbar focus, open popups, dialogs, gestures and high
contrast keep it visible. Automatic hiding can be disabled in preferences;
ordinary windows and other application sections retain the header.
.SH ACCESSIBILITY AND DISPLAYS
Preferences include text sizes from 12 to 96, high contrast, bold text,
line spacing, a low-vision preset, reading-column width and page brightness.
The Accessibility button in the reader header opens a compact menu with
text-size controls, high contrast, bold text, line spacing and the low-vision
preset. Appearance options are also available in preferences.
Interface text in application windows, dialogs and menus is 15% larger than
the system font and follows its family and desktop scale. Book text size
is configured separately.
Narration-language and text-size controls sit below their labels. The scrollbar
has its own space beside the content. The menu height fits the window; scroll
to reach the tools farther down.
The reading-area magnifier enlarges a region by 2 to 4 times without changing
text wrapping, the text-size setting or the original PDF/DjVu/CBZ layout. It follows
the mouse pointer over the reading area; otherwise it magnifies the center.
Enable it in the Accessibility menu for the current session; it starts disabled
again after restarting the application.
PDF/DjVu/CBZ use page zoom instead of changing text in the source image.
GTK handles display scaling. Only the current PDF/DjVu/CBZ page is rasterized;
the raster is capped at 4096 pixels on the longest edge and 12 MiPixels.
An 8K display or large zoom may therefore enlarge a bounded raster.
.SH NARRATION
Narration uses Piper exclusively. Install the piper-tts version 1.8.0 Python distribution
in a per-user virtual environment, normally
.IR ~/.local/share/malferma-libro/piper/ ,
and use paplay from pulseaudio-utils or aplay from alsa-utils for playback.
PIPER_PYTHON can select another Python interpreter with Piper installed.
The Debian system Python need not be changed; do not use sudo pip.
Changes to PIPER_PYTHON apply in a newly launched process.
Adding a voice model does not require a restart.
.PP
Voice models are downloaded separately at the user's request from the
application's catalog of models with checked free licenses. No model is
included in the application package. After installation, narration is offline
and does not send book text to a server. Models retain their own licenses.
Supported narration languages are Russian, Ukrainian, English, German,
French, Spanish, Italian and Portuguese, subject to a compatible installed
Piper model for the selected language. The checked download catalog covers
English, Ukrainian, German, French, Spanish and Italian. Russian and Portuguese
currently require a local .onnx model with its matching .onnx.json file;
the application does not certify the license of a user-selected model.
.PP
Settings, then Read aloud, provides voice selection, an explicit download
action, local model import and an offline sample preview. Selecting a voice
sets its language; an incompatible language change restores automatic voice
selection. Preview pauses book narration and leaves it paused.
Models are stored under voices/ in the application data directory.
Play, pause, resume and stop controls are in the header's Accessibility menu,
along with language selection and relative speed from 44 to 250 percent,
defaulting to 100 percent. Actual words per minute depend on the voice and text.
This does not restrict interface or book languages.
PDF/DjVu narration requires a text layer; OCR is not provided.
CBZ contains image pages and cannot be read aloud.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/malferma-libro/
Default directory for new installations. With an absolute XDG_DATA_HOME
the directory is instead
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/malferma-libro/ .
If the new directory does not exist but an otkrytaya-kniga directory already
exists under the same data home, that existing directory is reused.
User books are not automatically moved or deleted.
.TP
.I library.json / library.json.bak
Library metadata, reading status, last book, settings, bookmarks, notes and
reading positions / recovery copy.
.TP
.I books/
Managed book copies below the data directory.
.TP
.I voices/
Installed Piper voice models and their configuration and model-card records
below the data directory.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/malferma-libro/PIPER_LICENSES.md
Sources, licenses and review limits for Piper and the download catalog.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/malferma-libro/MANUAL.md
Complete Russian guide in the Debian package.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/malferma-libro/MANUAL.en.md
Complete English guide. German and Ukrainian versions are provided alongside it
as MANUAL.de.md and MANUAL.uk.md.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/malferma-libro/LICENSE
Full GPL v3 text. See LOGO_LICENSE.md for the artwork permission record,
FONT_LICENSES.md for fonts and LICENSE_AUDIT.md for the resource audit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
GTK 4 selects the graphical display from the process environment, including
DISPLAY and WAYLAND_DISPLAY. Display selection is not a reader command-line option.
.PP
The locale environment selects the language of concise help and of
.B \-\-manual
without an explicit language. The available guide languages are ru, en, de and uk;
other locales use English. The graphical guide's automatic selection instead
follows the application interface language.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Informational command completed successfully or graphical application exited normally.
.TP
.B 1
Required runtime or documentation resource could not be loaded.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
malferma-libro "Book with spaces.epub" "Another book.fb2"
malferma-libro \-\- \-book.txt
malferma-libro \-\-manual
malferma-libro \-\-manual=en
malferma-libro \-\-manual=ru
malferma-libro \-\-manual=de
malferma-libro \-\-manual=uk
malferma-libro \-\-license
.fi
.SH LIMITATIONS
HTML/XHTML (.html, .htm, .xhtml) is read as text without JavaScript, CSS,
browser layout or external-resource loading. Markdown (.md, .markdown) uses
CommonMark through markdown-it-py, version 3.0.0 or newer; GFM table and
footnote extensions are not enabled. Links retain labels, images retain
alt text and raw HTML is displayed literally. Each HTML/Markdown source file
is limited to 64 MiB and decoded text to 32 times 1024 times 1024 characters.
Markup complexity limits may reject a smaller file.
.PP
CBZ loads PNG/JPEG pages lazily in natural path/filename order, with 2 before
10. WebP requires an installed GdkPixbuf loader. Hidden and __MACOSX entries
are skipped; ComicInfo.xml can supply a title and author. CBZ is limited to
512 MiB per archive, 1 GiB expanded entries, 10,000 pages and 20,000 ZIP entries.
Each source image is limited to 32 MiB, 32 MiPixels and 16,384 pixels per edge.
Rendering is capped at 4096 pixels on the longest edge and 12 MiPixels.
.PP
EPUB CSS, inline images and interactive features are not reproduced in text mode.
Library cover extraction does not add inline image rendering to EPUB text.
DRM, authenticated catalogs and OPDS 2 are unsupported.
PDF/DjVu documents are limited to 64 MiB and 10,000 pages.
External-component DjVu documents must first be bundled.
